        <dc:title>Bucking the System</dc:title>
        <dc:creator opf:file-as="Cobolt, Dragon" opf:role="aut">Cobolt, Dragon</dc:creator>
        <dc:contributor opf:file-as="calibre" opf:role="bkp">calibre (3.42.0) [https://calibre-ebook.com]</dc:contributor>
        <dc:date>2018-04-27T00:00:00+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:description>&lt;p&gt;Patrick is a London-based freelance journalist and devoted boyfriend to the sensual jackal Nightshade, an exotic dancer and former dominatrix. An odd couple, Pat’s goofy wit and Nightshade’s alluring dominance make for an interesting and heartfelt mix.   &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pat thinks he’s hit the jackpot upon landing an interview with eccentric billionaire and tech mogul Ezra Maes. But while the deer is handsome, charming and utterly brilliant, Pat wasn’t expecting to stumble upon something both men had in common: a desire for the lovely Nightshade.   &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ever eager to please his lover, and curious to explore new frontiers in their bedroom play, Pat suggests Nightshade start up a relationship - not with Ezra, but rather his sex-hungry alter ego Buck. Massively endowed, confident and indulgent, Buck is everything Pat isn’t. But as Nightshade’s orgasms mount, so does Pat’s uncertainty and fear about what he’s brought on.   &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Has this new phase of Pat and Night’s relationship also become their last?   &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;BUCKING THE SYSTEM is a 40,000 word novella of lust, forbidden desire, mind games and true love. Based on the comic series Londoners by anthro artist Kadath.   &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DISCLAIMER: Contains cuckoldry, humiliation, femdom and emasculation.&lt;/p&gt;</dc:description>
